1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:07,417
Now that I see that you're
up ahead waiting there?

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:10,697
Hold on for me!

3
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:17,537
On this long journey that

4
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:19,297
we've only barely begun!

5
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:25,257
Friendship, love, courage,
and a little bit of fun!

6
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:28,997
These are the things.

7
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:33,377
That even as the years go by!

8
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:37,980
Will not ever vanish from our minds!

9
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:43,517
We are all pieces of
a single planet Earth!

10
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:49,660
Little by little we can
find each other's worth!

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,877
And as we see!

12
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:57,757
What sort of form we're meant to take!

13
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:01,900
All of us know the wind will
always keep on blowing away!

14
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:07,457
Feel the wind, feel it surround you!

15
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:09,620
As you finish what you've begun!

16
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:12,497
Look through that wind to dry!

17
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:14,177
All the tears as you're waiting!

18
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:16,077
The things you must overcome!

19
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:19,477
Join the quest, join the adventure!

20
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:21,917
Found in meeting somebody new!

21
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,180
We'll never stop for anything!

22
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:29,560
Now that I see that you're
up ahead waiting there!

23
00:01:30,940 --> 00:01:32,740
Hold on for me!

24
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:38,980
All the tears you shed will help
you to become so much stronger!

25
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:43,840
All the tears you shed
will help you to remember!

26
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:47,880
Everything, everything, everything!

27
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:50,060
Now and forever!

28
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:54,057
Whoa, whoa, whoa, yay!

29
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:57,577
Feel the wind, feel it surround you!

30
00:01:57,660 --> 00:01:59,700
As you finish what you've begun!

31
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:03,477
Look to the wind to dry all the tears!

32
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:06,177
As you're braving the
things you must overcome!

33
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:09,597
Join the quest, join the adventure!

34
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:12,077
Found in meeting somebody new!

35
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:15,197
We'll never stop for anything!

36
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:19,660
Now that I see that you're
up ahead waiting there!

37
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:22,820
Hold on for me!

38
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:52,660
Oh, my God.

39
00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:55,585
You're going to toss this
in the water or what?

40
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:59,005
I think you need to learn
your own limitations.

41
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:03,900
Stand firm!

42
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:05,375
Throw them overboard!

43
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:19,900
What's that?

44
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:24,960
It's Team Faye!

45
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:27,060
Behold my Fishman Karatis!

46
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,900
Watch your aim.

47
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:57,085
Oh, we were going to use
that ship, weren't we?

48
00:03:57,460 --> 00:04:00,840
Once I enter the water, I'm
afraid my strength runs wild.

49
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:12,740
Even if you made it outside, there's
no ship for you to escape on.

50
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:34,820
Don't do it, Straw Hat!

51
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:36,057
This is over the limit!

52
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:37,199
Run for your life!

53
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:38,670
Champion!

54
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:46,217
It had a good run, but my
wax can't help you anymore!

55
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:47,130
No more!

56
00:04:51,020 --> 00:04:52,640
What? What?

57
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:58,520
Scary!

58
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:03,180
Now perish.

59
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:06,620
Venom demon!

60
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:31,280
We better run!

61
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:32,461
Yeah, you think?

62
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,840
Hell's judgment, die!

63
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:47,620
He got me!

64
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:51,240
Please don't leave me! Help!

65
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,500
No, dammit, don't touch me!

66
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:58,005
Why would I have some clothes?

67
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:05,760
It looks like it's not just my wax!

68
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:08,177
That poison is spreading
over everything it touches!

69
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:10,319
Like a tidal wave of very bad news!

70
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:12,640
It was cool while it lasted me!

71
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,682
Yeah, that does look pretty bad!

72
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,460
Hurry up, straw boy!

73
00:06:25,660 --> 00:06:26,780
You gotta make it!

74
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:30,700
What about the ships?

75
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:34,177
I can hear gunfire, but the fog's
too heavy to make out anything.

76
00:06:34,260 --> 00:06:35,977
This is driving me crazy, man!

77
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:38,617
I know they're plenty
capable of stealing a ship,

78
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:42,053
but if the Marines delay them
long enough, we're screwed.

79
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:44,957
Sounds like they're pretty far out.

80
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,628
Even if they do nab a ship,

81
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:49,397
they'll have to drag it all the
way back here for us to get on it.

82
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:50,310
No way!

83
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:53,891
Magellan's probably going to
catch up to us any minute now.

84
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:57,277
I know Straw Hat survived
a fight with him once,

85
00:06:57,360 --> 00:07:01,007
but nobody can stop Magellan,
and this is taking awfully long.

86
00:07:04,780 --> 00:07:05,617
Straw Boy!

87
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:07,240
Teen Bay, hurry!

88
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:09,320
We're counting on you!

89
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:21,980
Do them all!

90
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,946
Don't let them take the ship!

91
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:34,340
Did his arm just turn into a knife?

92
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:36,080
What's up with this guy?

93
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:38,360
It's the Diced Ice Fruit.

94
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:44,280
I remember that bastard!

95
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:46,678
He's an assassin from the West Blue!

96
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:59,397
It's only a matter of time
before they take that ship!

97
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:01,660
I refuse to suffer that dishonor!

98
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:04,220
Have the cannon sink it, sir!

99
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:05,780
Ready, cannon!

100
00:08:10,340 --> 00:08:12,260
Oh no, not again?

101
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:19,417
The gunpowder!

102
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:21,600
It's so Jinbei, huh?

103
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:25,017
Keep him locked down.

104
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:26,060
Open fire!

105
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:29,437
He's right behind us!

106
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:31,220
We gotta run faster!

107
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:34,110
Jinbei?

108
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:52,880
Hey, you there, we're coming!

109
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:56,020
I hear straw boy!

110
00:08:57,920 --> 00:08:59,860
Run for it!

111
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:09,580
I don't know what that
thing is, but holy crap!

112
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:10,820
It's Magellan!

113
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:12,880
No, we're all gonna die!

114
00:09:15,020 --> 00:09:16,480
Did you get a ship?

115
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:17,740
Not yet!

116
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:20,417
We can't tell what the
heck's going on out there!

117
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:21,330
What?

118
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:29,300
Hell, a wing!

119
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:45,600
Is that Eva?

120
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:50,260
Don't scare us like that!

121
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:52,060
Oh, I made it.

122
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:53,760
Yay, it's nappy time.

123
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:56,160
No, not nappy time.

124
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:57,673
You have a head injury.

125
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:01,477
Thank goodness, you're alive.

126
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:04,820
I was so scared, I can't lose you!

127
00:10:07,740 --> 00:10:09,520
Still breathing, are you?

128
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:13,000
Hey, Straw Hat, call from Jinbei!

129
00:10:15,380 --> 00:10:17,180
A baby transponder snare?

130
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:20,569
Excellent work, gentlemen!

131
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:22,480
Now you show up.

132
00:10:23,820 --> 00:10:25,660
Luffy, you reached the exit?

133
00:10:26,100 --> 00:10:28,580
Uh-huh, but Magellan's still after us!

134
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:31,269
We're kind of running
out of places to run!

135
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:32,390
I see.

136
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:34,757
It took a while, but we do have a ship.

137
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:37,277
We'll be there soon, but
I need you to trust me.

138
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:38,419
Just keep running.

139
00:10:38,780 --> 00:10:40,417
Jump straight into the water.

140
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:43,029
That goes for you and
all of the prisoners.

141
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:44,971
Are you out of your mind?

142
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:47,257
You realize this is the clone belt, right?

143
00:10:47,340 --> 00:10:50,281
Sorry, but I don't have
time to explain right now.

144
00:10:53,060 --> 00:10:53,890
Let's do it!

145
00:10:53,973 --> 00:10:54,803
What?

146
00:10:54,886 --> 00:10:57,440
Three, I need another
wax thingy. We're dead!

147
00:10:57,740 --> 00:11:00,157
Either we drown or Medela destroys us!

148
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:02,457
Why do you trust that fish man anyway?

149
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:03,377
He's a warlord.

150
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:05,537
He's probably trying to curry
favor with the government.

151
00:11:05,620 --> 00:11:07,777
He's his friends are my friends, too.

152
00:11:07,860 --> 00:11:09,220
He won't let us down.

153
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:16,360
Into the water? Go ahead.

154
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:20,917
Let the Sea Kings eat you and save me
the trouble of cleaning up the mess.

155
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:21,830
Be careful!

156
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:24,477
Even a drop of that poison will kill you!

157
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:26,280
I got a beat!

158
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:31,470
Help!

159
00:11:31,553 --> 00:11:32,500
Judgment once more!

160
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:37,120
For dear!

161
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:40,280
This is as big as I can make it!

162
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:42,760
One candle wall coming right up!

163
00:11:45,340 --> 00:11:47,380
I got enough of your nonsense!

164
00:11:50,740 --> 00:11:52,220
Help! Help! Help!

165
00:11:54,680 --> 00:11:55,560
Jaaaa!

166
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:17,520
Whoa!

167
00:12:18,380 --> 00:12:19,900
They pushed him back!

168
00:12:33,440 --> 00:12:35,558
The poison is still seeping through!

169
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:38,231
Do we gotta dive into the water after all?

170
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:42,960
We did!

171
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:46,100
Hey, Eva! Wake up! Hurry!

172
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:47,797
We're in big trouble!

173
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:49,597
I need your fat head to do something!

174
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:53,268
I'm all tiny right now, and
you're the strongest person here!

175
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:54,510
What's that?

176
00:12:54,593 --> 00:12:55,797
We've got to get out of here!

177
00:12:55,880 --> 00:12:57,737
Who are you, baby straw boy?

178
00:12:57,820 --> 00:12:58,879
Do the wing thing!

179
00:12:59,260 --> 00:13:03,200
Do it! Okey-doke. No!
Please! All right! Help!

180
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:04,760
Here we go!

181
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:07,018
Wade, you're not in your right mind!

182
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:09,341
There's no way that's their plan.

183
00:13:09,780 --> 00:13:14,486
They won't survive two minutes in those
waters without a ship, and they know it.

184
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:17,980
Everybody grab onto
Eva's face! Do what? No!

185
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:20,435
Whatever you're trying to do, stop it!

186
00:13:22,020 --> 00:13:24,280
Hold on!

187
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:27,380
Help me!

188
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:32,160
I said stop!

189
00:13:46,300 --> 00:13:48,400
We're falling!

190
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:56,200
Something huge is under the
ship a swarm of sea kings.

191
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:07,217
We landed on something
look down i can't believe

192
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:11,457
this how are we still
alive i'm glad you made it.

193
00:14:11,540 --> 00:14:15,860
You must forgive me for making such
an outlandish request back there.

194
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:40,880
It's a school of whale sharks!

195
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:43,560
Jim Bay must have called them!

196
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:47,380
Ha-ha-ha!

197
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:48,900
Awesome!

198
00:14:56,380 --> 00:14:59,320
Now that is handy!

199
00:15:11,860 --> 00:15:13,000
Ha-ha!

200
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:15,020
All right!

201
00:15:15,860 --> 00:15:16,840
Yee-haw!

202
00:15:46,140 --> 00:15:48,620
Take that stupid poison guy.

203
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:51,437
She can't be fun too.

204
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:53,417
No more and fell down torture.

205
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:55,577
And I think I had almost given up hope!

206
00:15:55,660 --> 00:15:57,857
It's not time to celebrate yet.

207
00:15:57,940 --> 00:16:00,000
We still have a struggle ahead?

208
00:16:05,220 --> 00:16:06,660
We won!

209
00:16:07,140 --> 00:16:08,300
Thanks guys!

210
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:09,937
You whale sharks are awesome.

211
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:11,680
I'll never forget you!

212
00:16:12,780 --> 00:16:14,920
You saved our lives.

213
00:16:20,620 --> 00:16:22,817
I'd better start treatment on Inazuma.

214
00:16:22,900 --> 00:16:25,357
See what they've got
stashed in the sickbay.

215
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:26,270
Right.

216
00:16:29,380 --> 00:16:32,980
I'm never going back to that
hellhole as long as I live.

217
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,671
Yeah, man, no more crime.

218
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:36,958
I'm heading home to be a family man.

219
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:39,340
Suck it, diarrhea man.

220
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:41,060
We're finally free.

221
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:43,137
That's right, you're free.

222
00:16:43,220 --> 00:16:44,050
And thanks to who?

223
00:16:44,133 --> 00:16:45,620
Say it loud!

224
00:16:45,900 --> 00:16:47,300
Captain Buggy!

225
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:54,100
Resilient little insects. Come in.

226
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:55,792
This is Warden Magellan.

227
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:57,120
Bring me a ship.

228
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:59,680
I can still chase them down. Yes, sir!

229
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:02,077
Little do they know, for all their joy,

230
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:05,513
they've merely leapt from one
cage straight into another.

231
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:07,359
Rear Admiral, sir!

232
00:17:07,680 --> 00:17:10,877
We have repaired the battery that was
damaged by Koby in the last battle.

233
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:11,920
Good work.

234
00:17:12,260 --> 00:17:14,800
All ships, let's open fire!

235
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:27,540
They're gonna sink us!

236
00:17:28,100 --> 00:17:29,860
This is no way to die!

237
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:32,120
Come on, you guys, just let us go!

238
00:17:33,360 --> 00:17:35,040
They've got a whole fleet!

239
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:38,680
We're dead!

240
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:41,597
We've done well enough so far,

241
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:45,057
since all of their high-ranking officers
have been summoned to Marine Corps.

242
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:48,905
But we're still outnumbered, and
they won't let us go so easily.

243
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:57,097
Can't you see how I see your time?

244
00:17:57,180 --> 00:18:01,356
For filthy criminals such as you,
the Gates of Justice will never open!

245
00:18:09,060 --> 00:18:10,100
Oh crap!

246
00:18:10,420 --> 00:18:11,949
I forgot about that thing!

247
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:15,700
We're going to crash right
into it! He can't! Yeah!

248
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:16,910
Go Dancer!

249
00:18:16,993 --> 00:18:18,440
Whatever that guy said!

250
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:20,480
Hey, come on now!

251
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:23,177
What are we gonna do now, shark?

252
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:24,090
Keep sailing!

253
00:18:24,173 --> 00:18:25,577
You have lost your damn mind!

254
00:18:25,660 --> 00:18:26,957
You trying to get us killed?

255
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:28,800
Why the hell are you so calm?

256
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:30,273
We're all about to die!

257
00:18:42,380 --> 00:18:43,577
Protect the ship.

258
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:45,200
The gate can come next?

259
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:51,257
Why are we putting up with this crap?

260
00:18:51,340 --> 00:18:53,017
This is a navy ship too!

261
00:18:53,100 --> 00:18:55,297
Fire back, you imbeciles!

262
00:18:55,380 --> 00:18:58,097
I was just about to see
that on the cannons.

263
00:18:58,180 --> 00:19:00,097
Men, give them hell.

264
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:02,040
Roger that, Captain Foley!

265
00:19:10,780 --> 00:19:13,340
Take this! Save us!

266
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:15,820
I'm gone! Balloon!

267
00:19:16,580 --> 00:19:18,760
Look on that! Fire!

268
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:26,280
Where do they think they're going?

269
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:28,637
They expect the gate to
just open like magic.

270
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:30,340
Yeah, good luck with that.

271
00:19:30,520 --> 00:19:32,817
Magellan would have to hit
the switch for them himself.

272
00:19:32,900 --> 00:19:35,782
Guess the poor fools missed
the memo on that one.

273
00:19:41,340 --> 00:19:42,237
And fire!

274
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:44,040
Don't stop to their song!

275
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:50,100
The Gates of Justice! They're opening!

276
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:51,620
But why?

277
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:53,232
This doesn't make sense!

278
00:19:53,420 --> 00:19:54,580
Contact Impel Down!

279
00:19:57,700 --> 00:19:58,880
It's opening!

280
00:20:02,820 --> 00:20:04,740
Why is this happening?

281
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:06,950
A trap!

282
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:10,457
I don't know what's
going on and I don't care

283
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:15,960
as long as we're not dead and I can save
these! It's open! It's open! It's open!

284
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:20,440
They're escaping! Thanks!

285
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:24,860
Warden Magellan, hurry, please!

286
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:27,300
No, wait.

287
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,160
The gate.

288
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:36,440
Who authorized this?

289
00:20:40,420 --> 00:20:44,600
You're sure you want to open the
Gates of Justice at a time like this?

290
00:20:45,580 --> 00:20:47,100
Warden Magellan, sir?

291
00:20:47,520 --> 00:20:48,517
Of course I am.

292
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,659
Do you have any reason to doubt me?

293
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:52,780
No, I suppose not.

294
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:58,357
As soon as the prisoner's ship makes its
way through, I want you to close the gate.

295
00:20:58,440 --> 00:20:59,270
Understood?

296
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:00,760
If you say so, sir.

297
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:08,860
We haven't lost them
yet. Take the ship. Fire!

298
00:21:10,780 --> 00:21:12,560
Did Magellan order this?

299
00:21:12,740 --> 00:21:13,858
What's he thinking?

300
00:21:14,780 --> 00:21:16,660
Has anyone contacted the ward?

301
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:18,468
Something isn't right here.

302
00:21:18,580 --> 00:21:19,933
Actually, sir, I agree.

303
00:21:20,060 --> 00:21:22,589
We saw the warden at
the pier a moment ago.

304
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:27,525
The thing is, he seemed as confused about
it as we are and just took off running.

305
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:33,376
When I find out who's responsible
for this, I'm gonna wring their neck.

306
00:21:34,340 --> 00:21:35,680
Damn it, control room!

307
00:21:35,940 --> 00:21:37,060
What are you doing?

308
00:21:37,380 --> 00:21:39,792
Who told you to open the gate of justice?

309
00:21:40,620 --> 00:21:42,400
Wait, a warden?

310
00:21:54,780 --> 00:21:59,117
All this time you knew and that's why

311
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:05,340
you didn't stop you bastard that's me!

312
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:12,437
I got you you silly man
didn't learn your lesson

313
00:22:12,520 --> 00:22:15,640
the first time did you
he was a fake all along?

314
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:23,390
Look!

315
00:22:23,473 --> 00:22:24,817
They're trying to close the gate on us!

316
00:22:24,900 --> 00:22:25,730
That's good.

317
00:22:25,813 --> 00:22:28,677
As long as we can make it through in
time that it'll slam in their faces,

318
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:29,897
then we'll be free to go!

319
00:22:29,980 --> 00:22:30,810
Damn it!

320
00:22:30,893 --> 00:22:32,796
Vaughn was with us just a second ago!

321
00:22:33,640 --> 00:22:36,820
He helped us fight Eva,
and he helped us escape!

322
00:22:37,160 --> 00:22:40,337
He saved me from that poison and
cheered for me the whole way!

323
00:22:40,420 --> 00:22:42,557
He's my friend, and you
want to go without him?

324
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:43,640
There's no time!

325
00:22:43,860 --> 00:22:46,331
We can't just leave him to die back there!

326
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:47,430
You listen.

327
00:22:47,513 --> 00:22:51,612
The only way anyone could make it,
we've left immeasurable comrades behind.

328
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:56,477
Do you want to go back and fight Magellan
again and risk losing even more friends?

329
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:58,797
What if we hadn't stayed
behind to open the gate?

330
00:22:58,880 --> 00:23:00,417
Then where would we be right now?

331
00:23:00,500 --> 00:23:01,580
Dead or worse?

332
00:23:05,460 --> 00:23:08,680
If anyone can get the gate
open for you guys, it's me.

333
00:23:09,080 --> 00:23:11,551
Don't worry, your pretty little blue head.

334
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:17,160
I don't doubt that you can
succeed, but then what?

335
00:23:17,580 --> 00:23:20,260
Let's not ask silly questions, all right?

336
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:26,280
But do me a favor and don't tell
Strawboy until communications are cut.

337
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:30,860
Swans never die and never say goodbye.

338
00:23:36,120 --> 00:23:37,660
It's still connected.

339
00:23:41,240 --> 00:23:43,946
Baby transponder snails
have limited coverage.

340
00:23:44,340 --> 00:23:47,660
Once the gate closes, you
won't be able to speak to him.

341
00:23:52,880 --> 00:23:54,560
You dare to mark the warden?

342
00:23:54,660 --> 00:23:55,777
You'll pay for this!

343
00:23:55,860 --> 00:23:58,448
I knew memorizing your
face was a good idea.

344
00:23:59,460 --> 00:24:00,960
Wake up, you imbecile!

345
00:24:01,260 --> 00:24:02,777
What the hell happened here?

346
00:24:02,860 --> 00:24:04,389
Please, you're choking me!

347
00:24:07,100 --> 00:24:08,180
And touch. Watch!

348
00:24:10,260 --> 00:24:11,120
Curse you!

349
00:24:12,460 --> 00:24:13,720
God! God!

350
00:24:15,820 --> 00:24:17,080
Strawboy? Hey!

351
00:24:17,280 --> 00:24:18,337
Can you still hear me?

352
00:24:18,420 --> 00:24:19,250
It's Luffy!

353
00:24:19,460 --> 00:24:20,480
Are you nuts?

354
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:22,033
Why are you doing this?

355
00:24:22,980 --> 00:24:25,080
It's just like last time!

356
00:24:26,420 --> 00:24:29,697
Jibe, you promised you weren't
far to tell him until later!

357
00:24:29,780 --> 00:24:31,662
This is the last thing I wanted!

358
00:24:33,360 --> 00:24:36,360
We were supposed to break
out together, weren't we?

359
00:24:36,900 --> 00:24:37,780
Damn it!

360
00:24:37,940 --> 00:24:40,469
How many times do you
have to save me, huh?

361
00:24:42,860 --> 00:24:45,520
I was there! Say something! Answer!

362
00:24:46,400 --> 00:24:47,580
He saved us.

363
00:24:48,420 --> 00:24:49,780
We're only free now.

364
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:54,620
Because he stayed behind in that
hell. Come on! Brother, please!

365
00:24:54,760 --> 00:24:56,277
We just want to talk to you!

366
00:24:56,360 --> 00:24:57,737
Let us know you're alive, okay?

367
00:24:57,820 --> 00:24:58,650
Say something!

368
00:24:59,160 --> 00:24:59,990
Run!

369
00:25:05,980 --> 00:25:07,140
Mr. Two!

370
00:25:08,240 --> 00:25:10,260
Oh, dare you, Mr. Two!

371
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:12,980
Before I can tell you, I'm sorry!

372
00:25:13,640 --> 00:25:14,470
Ha-ha!

373
00:25:15,720 --> 00:25:17,440
Bond boy! Fire!

374
00:25:18,140 --> 00:25:20,316
Don't let them get through that gate!

375
00:25:20,420 --> 00:25:21,832
Blow them to smotheries!

376
00:25:22,900 --> 00:25:23,730
Bond!

377
00:25:23,820 --> 00:25:25,080
It made me!

378
00:25:28,060 --> 00:25:29,540
This is it.

379
00:25:29,840 --> 00:25:31,640
The gate's about to close.

380
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:38,480
We have to go.

381
00:25:45,340 --> 00:25:47,340
So thank you.

382
00:25:57,220 --> 00:25:59,520
We'll never forget you!

383
00:26:10,980 --> 00:26:12,560
Strawboy! I'm here!

384
00:26:13,140 --> 00:26:13,970
Strawboy!

385
00:26:14,660 --> 00:26:16,460
Five days! Save him!

386
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:17,940
And don't look bad!

387
00:26:23,620 --> 00:26:25,657
I know you can do it.

388
00:26:25,740 --> 00:26:27,877
And you have lots of friends.

389
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:29,080
To help you.

390
00:26:30,120 --> 00:26:33,957
The gate is closing.

391
00:26:34,040 --> 00:26:35,477
Keep hiring!

392
00:26:35,560 --> 00:26:36,840
Take them out.

393
00:26:43,340 --> 00:26:45,420
Did you miss me, old pal?

394
00:26:46,540 --> 00:26:47,370
No!

395
00:26:47,453 --> 00:26:48,283
Yeah, we did it!

396
00:26:48,366 --> 00:26:49,300
We really did it!

397
00:26:49,720 --> 00:26:52,080
Oh, stop pulling my tail!

398
00:26:57,260 --> 00:26:59,900
Strawboy, I've come here to rescue you!

399
00:27:02,380 --> 00:27:05,440
In the name of our everlasting friendship!

400
00:27:08,520 --> 00:27:10,080
Hang in there!

401
00:27:11,080 --> 00:27:13,240
You have to live!

402
00:27:14,320 --> 00:27:15,280
Strawboy!

403
00:27:17,660 --> 00:27:21,800
Swans never die and never say goodbye.

404
00:27:24,200 --> 00:27:25,030
Rawr!

405
00:27:32,180 --> 00:27:34,860
I can't believe this.

406
00:27:36,220 --> 00:27:37,500
Take out a way!

407
00:27:38,240 --> 00:27:39,680
We owe him our lives.

408
00:27:39,920 --> 00:27:40,917
We're finally free.

409
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:44,737
If it wasn't for him, we'd be sitting
at the bottom of the ocean right now.

410
00:27:44,820 --> 00:27:49,860
Even in the depths of hell, the flower
of friendship shall still bloom,

411
00:27:50,340 --> 00:27:52,440
flames licking at its stem.

412
00:27:52,820 --> 00:27:56,600
And on the sands of the river
where souls part from the living,

413
00:27:57,020 --> 00:28:01,220
it sheds a solitary petal,
leaving it behind as a memento.

414
00:28:01,600 --> 00:28:05,240
So let us vow that we shall
make it bloom again someday.

415
00:28:06,040 --> 00:28:07,800
Oh, come my way!

416
00:28:25,160 --> 00:28:28,000
Any last words before I eliminate you?

417
00:28:28,700 --> 00:28:29,900
Have at me!

418
00:28:31,140 --> 00:28:34,920
Let us meet again in the
garden of O Come My Way.

419
00:28:36,440 --> 00:28:37,660
And suddenly,

420
00:28:37,940 --> 00:28:39,240
in one fell swoop,

421
00:28:39,440 --> 00:28:45,340
the number of prisoners that had escaped
from Impel Downjump from 1 to 241.

422
00:28:46,860 --> 00:28:47,860
And yet,

423
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:52,706
this is only the beginning of a turn of
events that will shake the entire world.

424
00:28:54,380 --> 00:28:57,020
The public execution of Portgas D.

425
00:28:57,140 --> 00:29:00,540
Ace will take place in four hours.
